#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; is an educational programming environment based on the <link "
"linkend=\"what-is-logo\">&logo;</link> programming language. The goal of "
"&kturtle; is to make programming as easy and accessible as possible. This "
"makes &kturtle; suitable for teaching kids the basics of math, geometry "
"and... programming. The commands used to program are in the style of the "
"&logo; programming language. The unique feature of the &logo; programming "
"language is that the commands are often translated into the speaking "
"language of the programmer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; is named after <quote>the turtle</quote> that plays a central role "
"in the programming environment. The user programs the turtle, using the "
"&logo; commands, to draw a picture on <link linkend=\"the-canvas\">the "
"canvas</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is &logo;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first version &logo; programming language was created by Seymour Papert "
"of MIT Artificial Intelligence Laboratory in 1967 as an offshoot of the LISP "
"programming language. From then many versions of &logo; have been released. "
"By 1980 &logo; was gaining momentum, with versions for MSX, Commodore, "
"Atari, Apple II and IBM PC systems. These versions were mainly for "
"educational purposes. LCSI released <application>&Mac;&logo;</application> "
"in 1985 as a tool for professional programmers, but it never caught on. MIT "
"is still maintaining a site on &logo; which can be found on <ulink url="
"\"http://el.media.mit.edu/logo-foundation/\">http://el.media.mit.edu/logo- "
"foundation/</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Today there are several versions of &logo; around which can easily be found "
"on <ulink url=\"http://el.media.mit.edu/logo-foundation/\">MIT's &logo; "
"site</ulink> and by a simple <ulink url=\"http://www.google.com/search?q=logo"
"+programming+kids\">Google search</ulink>. This version of &logo; "
"(&kturtle;) is only focused on the educational qualities of the programming "
"language and will not try to suit professional programmers' needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Features of &kturtle;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kturtle; has some nice features that make starting to program a breeze. See "
"here some of the highlights of &kturtle; feature set:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An integrated interpreter (no extra dependencies) that uses Ruby files for "
"the command translations, supports user defined functions and dynamic type "
"switching."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "The execution can be slown down, paused or stopped at any time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A powerful editor for the &logo; commands with intuitive syntax "
"highlighting, line numbering and more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"the-canvas\">The canvas</link> can be saved as an image or "
"printed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Context help for all commands: Just press <keysym>F2</keysym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kturtle; commands are fully translatable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An error dialog that links the error messages to the mistakes in the program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simplified programming terminology."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many integrated, internationalized example programs make it easy to get "
"started."
msgstr ""

